Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)

The following indicators were identified during the investigation:

* Source IP Address: 198.51.100.45
* Compromised IAM Identity: medvitals-deploy-bot
* Assumed IAM Role: AdminFullAccess
* Suspicious User Agent: python-requests/2.28.1
* Affected S3 Bucket: medvitals-patient-records
* Suspicious File: exfil/bulk-export-20260630.tar.gz
* AWS API Calls Observed:
    * AssumeRole
    * ListBuckets
    * PutObject
    * GetObject

Root Cause

The investigation determined that the primary root cause was an overly permissive IAM wildcard policy, which allowed the deployment bot to assume the AdminFullAccess role.

This excessive permission violated the Principle of Least Privilege and enabled the attacker to:

* Escalate privileges
* Access sensitive AWS resources
* Enumerate S3 buckets
* Stage sensitive data
* Exfiltrate confidential patient records

